node_modules/
dist/
.history/
.astro/
.DS_Store
*.local
.playwright-mcp

# Never commit credentials. This app is designed so a token never reaches a server, and the repo is
# public — an API token that lands here is exposed to everyone, permanently, even if later deleted.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.token
public/_devtoken.json

# `capture.test.ts` always writes here, and the file is a staging area rather than a fixture:
# the three committed fixtures are made by renaming it. Left tracked it gets swept into whatever
# commit is open when a capture runs, which is how a 25k-line orphan reached the history once.
#
# Globbed over the spec because this pattern had already gone dead once: it named
# `src/lib/__fixtures__/`, a directory that no longer exists, while the capture writes to
# `src/specs/windwalker/__fixtures__/` — so the one file it exists to keep out was tracked again, and
# a second spec's capture would have been too.
src/specs/*/__fixtures__/analysis.json

# `wrangler pages dev dist` writes temp JavaScript here while exercising `public/_headers`, and
# oxlint then fails on files nobody wrote.
.wrangler/

# Claude Code worktrees live under .claude/worktrees/ and must never be tracked.
.claude/worktrees/

# The working plan for the multi-spec migration. Deliberately untracked: it is a scratchpad for
# whoever is mid-migration, not a document the repository maintains. `docs/conventions.md` and
# `.claude/skills/wcl-analyzer/SKILL.md` are the durable records.
docs/plan.md

# The working plan for the reader-voice pass, untracked for the same reason and by the same rule.
# It was briefly tracked — Phase 1 of the plan told a lane to `git add` it — and that was the wrong
# call: a phased migration plan is a scratchpad for whoever is mid-migration. The standard it was
# migrating toward is the durable record, and that lives in `docs/conventions.md`.
#
# The skill beside it is ignored on purpose and for a different reason: it is an authoring aid for an
# agent working in this checkout — a procedure to load, not an artifact the repository ships — and it
# is the whole `.claude/skills/` story here, where only `wcl-analyzer/SKILL.md` is tracked.
#
# **What that cost, and how it was paid.** `docs/conventions.md` and
# `src/specs/__tests__/readerVoice.test.ts` source every corpus rate they quote — "243/100k across 6
# of 6 authors", the 18,889-word sample, the em-dash count in the genre — from the skill's
# `references/audience-wow-players.md`, so for a while two tracked files rested their arguments on a
# path a clone does not have. The measurements are evidence rather than procedure, so they moved to
# `docs/audience-wow-players.md` and are tracked there; the skill keeps its own copy for the agent.
# This comment used to end "both of which stay tracked", which was never true of the second one.
docs/tone-of-voice-migration.md
.claude/skills/tone-of-voice/

# Throwaway vitest configs for one-off measurement probes. The technique is documented in the
# lane briefs: a config at the repo root pointing at a scratchpad test, deleted after the run. A
# forgotten one used to fail `npm run check` for every other lane and could be swept into a commit
# by a `git add -A`.
probe*.config.mjs
